# BRQOSH — Schema Governance Law v17

**Cloud Code:** `docs/CLOUD-CODE-AGENT-GUIDE.md` · Sibling ERP schema law — not CognitiveQa primary

## Golden Rule

**Every schema change must pass SQLite AND PostgreSQL before ✅.**

No column, table, or migration is "closed" on SQLite alone. PostgreSQL = production. SQLite = fast dev/CI. **Both are mandatory.**

---

## 60-Second Agent Diagnosis

```
PG error in Desktop/test
├─ "Unsupported PostgreSQL column type"?
│  └─ unregistered type → AllowedPgTypes + SchemaSqlGuardTests + PG re-test
├─ column in SQLite not PG (or reverse)?
│  └─ drift → sync ApplySqlitePatchesAsync + ApplyPostgreSqlPatchesAsync
├─ EF Entity changed without SchemaUpdater?
│  └─ add incremental migration — EnsureCreated insufficient for old DBs
└─ SQLite PASS only?
   └─ NOT CLOSED — run schema-gate-pg.ps1
```

---

## Recurring Failures (do not repeat)

| Symptom | Root cause | Agent action |
|---------|------------|--------------|
| `Unsupported PostgreSQL column type: character varying(128)` | PG type not in registry | register + theory + PG test |
| V12 passes SQLite · Desktop fails PG | SQLite-only column | sync both paths |
| agent says "complete" | CI = SQLite in-memory | state SQLite ✅ / PG ✅ or ❌ explicitly |
| EF ↔ SchemaUpdater drift | separate DDL paths | review all three: EF + Updater + Guard |

